Removing branding, changing names, modifying code, or bundling the Software
with other components does not avoid these conditions. An external offering
is not Internal Use merely because it is free, bundled with another service,
or charged for indirectly. A separate commercial agreement must expressly
grant the applicable external-offering and distribution rights.

